laurel 2911: kern.laurel_stats, the data of the XNUtils app (docs/laurel_sprout/xnutils.md).

A read-only string sysctl for every user. It parses the console ring that sweet_ufs.c keeps anyway, only when somebody reads it and
in the log thread that wakes every 10 s anyway (bsd/dev/laurel_stats_core.h, host test scripts/laurel/xnutils-test.sh): last state
line per feature, last line per driver + count, crashes by process, processes with a Metal or GPU device. Runs of 14+ digits become
'#'. Live values from variables the drivers keep: laurel_thermal_stats, laurel_gpu_dcvs_stats, laurel_wifi_stats. No hook in the print
path, no new poll, no register read. Kill switch laurelstats=0. Line: LAUREL STATS: on|off.

